  "reviewedSceneLanguage": {
    "magnetization.ponder.mr_fluid_bridge.header": "Build a switchable MR Fluid bridge",
    "magnetization.ponder.mr_fluid_bridge.text_1": "Pour MR Fluid over a temporary floor between the banks. With no redstone or magnetic field, the source spreads into flowing cells.",
    "magnetization.ponder.mr_fluid_bridge.text_2": "Apply redstone to harden the fluid, then remove the temporary floor. The rigid cells form a walkable bridge and still conduct redstone.",
    "magnetization.ponder.mr_fluid_bridge.text_3": "Add a nearby magnet, then remove redstone. The magnetic field keeps the bridge rigid on its own.",
    "magnetization.ponder.mr_fluid_bridge.text_4": "Remove the magnet too. With both activations gone, original sources return and the fluid flows again. Flowing cells do not become extra sources.",
    "magnetization.ponder.field_strength_control.header": "Balance field strength",
    "magnetization.ponder.field_strength_control.text_1": "This Samarium-Cobalt magnet starts at MEDIUM. The examples use the default enabled Halbach bonus.",
    "magnetization.ponder.field_strength_control.text_2": "One face-adjacent magnet with the same pole adds one tier: MEDIUM becomes STRONG.",
    "magnetization.ponder.field_strength_control.text_3": "Two aligned neighbors still give only one bonus tier. The field remains STRONG.",
    "magnetization.ponder.field_strength_control.text_4": "Three aligned neighbors give two bonus tiers: EXTREME. Four through six give the same bonus; EXTREME is the ceiling.",
    "magnetization.ponder.field_strength_control.text_5": "Remove the aligned neighbors to return to the base MEDIUM field before adding dampeners.",
    "magnetization.ponder.field_strength_control.text_6": "One face-adjacent Hematite block lowers MEDIUM to WEAK. Each additional touching face lowers another tier.",
    "magnetization.ponder.field_strength_control.text_7": "A second Hematite block lowers WEAK to NONE: complete suppression. Dampeners must touch the emitter, not just each other.",
    "magnetization.ponder.magnetizing_equipment.header": "Stamp equipment polarity",
    "magnetization.ponder.magnetizing_equipment.text_1": "Open an Electromagnet and put metal equipment in its magnetizing slot. N, S and Clear act on that item, not on the emitter pole.",
    "magnetization.ponder.magnetizing_equipment.text_2": "Choose N and equip the helmet. The NORTH magnet repels the NORTH-stamped wearer; an opposite SOUTH field attracts them.",
    "magnetization.ponder.magnetizing_equipment.text_3": "Choose S and equip it again. The same NORTH field now attracts the SOUTH-stamped wearer. The arrows illustrate the response.",
    "magnetization.ponder.magnetizing_equipment.text_4": "Choose Clear to remove the stamp. Metal armor still contributes susceptibility; without other stamps the wearer defaults to NORTH. Clear does not make metal nonmagnetic."
  },
